Z||000002||yo_sweet||11-21-2001||11:14 AM||||no it runs good when started its an 86 se v6<BR>its got 112km on the origonal motor and tranny,it used to start right on the click <BR>but now it takes a bit to turn it over when its cold<p>[This message has been edited by yo_sweet (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierocritter||11-21-2001||11:22 AM||||I had a very similar problem. My car would br very hard to start when it was cold. Replaced the cold start switch in the intake manifold, right next to the fan switch. the switch controls the seventh injector that is used on cold starts. I don't know if you have a starter problem or electrical problem so I cannot diagnose. Just saying this is what happened to me!||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||11-21-2001||12:54 PM||||Cold start switch was my first guess, too, although I haven't had the same problem.<P>I know what you mean about starting "right on the click" - my 1986 SE V6 still fires up instantly.  About as fast as you can possibly bump the starter and let up on the key.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||11-22-2001||01:21 AM||||I find that my 86 SE-V6 starts up very good if I do the following.<BR>Turn the ign switch on and do not fasten your seat belt yet. the chime will chim 5 times then start your car this gives the fuel pump time to build up pressure. fasten your seat belt and drive away.||||reg||1
Z||000006||reddog||11-22-2001||02:58 AM||||If it tries to start but dies immediately then it could be your Coolant Tempurature Sensor!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||watts||11-22-2001||03:35 PM||||This should almost go as it's own message, but...  A lot of people have been wondering how to diagnose the cold start valve, how it's set up, etc.  Well...  see these two (rather large) pages.  Might want to just save and print them off.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/coldstart-1.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/coldstart-2.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||SLYGUY||11-22-2001||11:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<P><B>my 1986 SE V6 still fires up instantly.  About as fast as you can possibly bump the starter and let up on the key.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>My 88GT is the same way. I've even found it to start this quickly even when I don't let the fuel pump prime the cylinders first. <P>Sly<BR>||||reg||1
